//? Title: Point geometry:tensor distances and frozen neighborhood derivatives
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Deterministic farthest-point sampling and strict-radius groups prepare PointNet++ neighborhoods. Complete plotted fixtures,duplicate gather adjoints and all-coordinate checks make the discrete and differentiable behavior explicit.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.10_3d_and_video_convolutions/point_geometry.cpp`.

> The method

Compute distances and input-order ranking with tensors,retain categorical center/neighbor IDs,and differentiate through gathered features and centroid-relative coordinates with those choices frozen. Plot every declared fixture point and verify ties,padding,translation and explicit errors.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/point_geometry_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/point_geometry_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/point_geometry_concept.tikz > build/point_geometry_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/point_geometry_concept.svg build/point_geometry_concept.dvi > build/point_geometry_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
