> Verification and limits

Four native tests execute the original complete fixture,compare every FPS,
radius count/index and gathered value with retained independent host source
across12three-batch clouds and nine radius/slot combinations,and check exact
duplicate scatter,detached choices and invalid inputs. Public examples,
standalone inclusion,the original program and documentation hovers pass.
These supporting operations do not train or validate a classifier. Their
frozen-choice derivatives apply within a fixed discrete neighborhood,not
through selection discontinuities. Mesh-based model reports remain separate.

> Conclusion

Tensor geometry preserves the source neighborhood policy while gather/subtraction retain useful gradients. Complete fixtures and independent host checks establish these primitive contracts without a fitted classifier or benchmark claim.

> References

- [Qi et al.(2017),PointNet++:Deep Hierarchical Feature Learning on Point Sets in a Metric Space](https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.02413).
